Draw an instance batch with the bases of its first draw. A draw.begin with InstanceId::First,
then pairs with InstanceId::Subsequent, is drawn as its first draw at once and as one instanced
draw in DrawDeferred, which read the base instance and base vertex from the registers at that
time. OoT's text macros (0x1e6) draw each line's glyphs this way with the line's first glyph as
base instance, then reset the register before the macro ends: every line's batch drew the glyphs
of the start of the glyph buffer, and only each line's first letter was right. The bases of the
batch's first draw are now kept for the batch.

